/-
  LeanBCH.Validation.CostDifferential — the consensus op-cost model, DIFFERENTIALLY pinned to libauth.
  (Extracted from VM/CostDifferential.lean into the validation layer: it is pure build-time validation
  — a `#eval` guard, no proofs — so it belongs beside the other known-answer tests, importing the
  model rather than living in it.)

  The five raw op-cost metrics (arithmeticCost, hashDigestIterations, signatureCheckCount,
  stackPushedBytes, evaluatedInstructionCount) that `operationCost` sums are cross-checked, at BUILD
  TIME, against the pinned reference @bitauth/libauth 3.1.0-next.8 running the SAME scripts on its
  BCH-2026 VM. The expected numbers below are libauth's ACTUAL output, MACHINE-GENERATED by
  `conformance/cost/gen.mjs` (never hand-typed) from `conformance/cost/battery.txt`; the `#eval`
  guard runs each script through LeanBCH's metered VM (`runScript`) and throws on ANY metric
  mismatch. So a cost-CONSTANT transcription slip in the model (e.g. an arithmeticCost or
  stackPushedBytes miscount) FAILS `lake build` — closing the audit's "self-consistent witness"
  gap with an independent, reproducible differential. Regenerate: `node conformance/cost/gen.mjs`.

  SCOPE (honest): this differential exercises the arith / hash / push / instruction-count tiers
  across operand widths and all five hash ops. It does NOT cover `signatureCheckCount`'s 26000
  multiplier (a CHECKSIG differential needs real secp256k1 signatures, outside this mathlib-free
  core — see Extended.lean; sigcheck COUNTING is witnessed by the mock-oracle KATs there, and the
  26000 rate is exercised end-to-end by the vmb_2026 corpus boundary families). libauth's
  `metrics.operationCost` uses the STANDARD hash factor H=192; the CONSENSUS factor H=64 is the
  epoch choice in `Epoch.operationCost` — so only the raw metrics (which the formula multiplies)
  are compared here, and they match EXACTLY on all vectors below.
-/
import LeanBCH.VM.Verify
import LeanBCH.Validation.Fixtures

namespace LeanBCH.Validation
open LeanBCH LeanBCH.VM LeanBCH.VM.State LeanBCH.Tx LeanBCH.Cost LeanBCH.Crypto

/-- libauth 3.1.0-next.8 BCH-2026 op-cost vectors, machine-generated by `conformance/cost/gen.mjs`:
    `(script bytes, arithmeticCost, hashDigestIterations, signatureCheckCount, stackPushedBytes,
    evaluatedInstructionCount)`. Do not hand-edit — regenerate from `conformance/cost/battery.txt`. -/
def costVectors : List (LeanBCH.Bytes × Nat × Nat × Nat × Nat × Nat) :=
[
